# funkysi1701.com (Hugo blog) — core rules

Portable onboarding: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). PR checklist: [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](../../CONTRIBUTING.md). Copilot detail: [`.github/copilot-instructions.md`](../../.github/copilot-instructions.md). Path-scoped rules in [`.cursor/rules/`](.) activate for content, tests, layouts, and parkrun.

Prefer matching existing patterns (Hugo TOML front matter in `+++` fences, site overrides under root `layouts/` and `static/`).

## Source of truth and generated output

- **Hugo content and config:** Edit Markdown under `content/`, site parameters under `config/_default/` (and `config/development/`, `config/staging/`, `config/production/` when environment-specific). Active theme: `config/_default/config.toml` (`theme = 'hugo-theme-bootstrap'`), a **frozen fork of hugo-theme-bootstrap v0.65.1**. Production Hugo does not run theme npm/webpack. Do not rebase onto upstream v1.
- **Theme vs site overrides:** Prefer root `layouts/`, `assets/`, and `static/` over editing `themes/hugo-theme-bootstrap/`. See `hugo-layouts.mdc` when changing templates.
- **Build output:** `public/` is generated — not source of truth. Production builds use Dockerized Hugo with `--minify --environment production` (`.github/workflows/azure-static-web-apps-victorious-pebble-0b8f90e03.yml`). **blog-dev** deploys (`hugo_environment: development` via `swa-deploy-nonprod.yml`) also pass `--buildFuture` so future-dated posts appear on preview; staging/production do not.
- **New posts:** Always set `draft = false`. Review unpublished work on **https://blog-dev.funkysi1701.com** (`feature/*` and `develop`); production is `main`. Do not use Hugo `draft = true` as the unpublished flag — see `content-posts.mdc`.
- **Parkrun page:** Generated block in `content/parkrun.md` — see `parkrun-generated.mdc`; do not hand-edit between markers.
- **Home popular links:** `data/home_popular.toml` drives the home strip. `home-popular-update.yml` refreshes its URLs weekly from Cloudflare Web Analytics through `scripts/home-popular/run.mjs` and opens a PR into `develop`; editorial titles are preserved.
- **Analytics:** Production engagement KPIs use **Lite Analytics via Cloudflare Zaraz** (not Hugo). Do not embed `lite.js` in templates while Zaraz injects it. Inventory and keep/disable decisions: [`README.md`](../../README.md#analytics-cloudflare-zaraz). Cloudflare Web Analytics (separate beacon) feeds the home Popular strip.
- **Git submodules:** CI checks out with `submodules: true`. Keep submodule config in sync if used.
- **Azure Static Web Apps:** `staticwebapp.config.json` is copied into `public/` on every SWA deploy; keep routing and headers aligned with the built site. After edits, run `npm run check:swa-config` (CI: `swa-config.yml`). Required `globalHeaders` include HSTS, frame/MIME/referrer/permissions policies, and Content-Security-Policy. Do not add SPA `navigationFallback` to `/index.html` (soft-404 homepage); use `responseOverrides["404"]` → `/404.html`.

## Security and configuration

- `.env` tracks non-secret shared config (e.g. `HUGO_VERSION`). **Do not** commit secrets, API keys, or deploy tokens. Azure SWA deploy token lives only in GitHub Actions secrets.
- Cloudflare automation keeps `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` in GitHub Actions secrets; account/site tags are repository variables.
- **Giscus** and similar use public repo identifiers; avoid private tokens in `config/` or front matter.

## Local development

- **Hugo:** `hugo server -D` from repo root, or Docker Compose (`docker-compose.yml`) / commands in `README.md`. Hugo version from `HUGO_VERSION` in `.env`.
- **Images:** Static binaries under `static/` (site root). Stable paths for external links.
- **Node:** After changing `package.json` or `package-lock.json`, run `npm ci` before `npm test` (matches GitHub Actions).

## Branches and deploy

| Branch | Target |
|--------|--------|
| **`main`** | Production — GHA → Azure SWA (`www.funkysi1701.com`) |
| **`develop`** | Non-prod — GHA → SWA dev + test (`blog-dev`, `blog-test`) |
| **`feature/*`** | GHA → SWA dev only |

No **`dev`** branch — use **`develop`**. `.github/workflows/auto-pr.yml` can open or refresh **develop → main**.

## Documentation

- Tracked **`*.md`** is part of the repo contract. When a change affects documented behaviour, update every affected Markdown file in the same change.
- Keep **`AGENTS.md`**, **`CONTRIBUTING.md`**, **`README.md`**, **`.github/copilot-instructions.md`**, and **`.cursor/rules/`** aligned when workflows, branches, testing, or automation shift. Do not add new Markdown files unless the user or task asks.

## Scope

Make the smallest change that satisfies the task. Do not refactor unrelated code or add dependencies without clear need.
